# Build contexts became the repo root when authbridge/ was flattened, so the
# things that were previously outside every context are now inside one.
#
# NOTE ON ANCHORING — the opposite of .gitignore. Docker matches each pattern
# against the file's WHOLE path relative to the context root, so a bare `venv`
# catches ./venv and nothing else; a nested tests/__pycache__ sails straight
# past it. Recursive patterns need an explicit `**/`. The flip side is that a
# bare name here cannot accidentally match a directory deeper in the tree the
# way it does in .gitignore, so the root-level entries below need no leading
# slash to stay anchored.
.git
.worktrees
.superpowers
bin
dist
.cpex-ffi

# Caches and virtualenvs, which show up at any depth (tests/__pycache__ does).
**/venv
**/.venv
**/__pycache__
**/.pytest_cache
**/.ruff_cache
**/.mypy_cache
**/node_modules
**/*.test

# Compiled Go binaries. This mirrors .gitignore, which Docker does not read: on
# any machine that has run `go build`, these are ~63MB of stale binaries that
# would otherwise be shipped into the build context and then ignored by the
# builder, which recompiles from source anyway.
#
# `cmd/*/cortex*` catches the in-package builds (cmd/cortex/
# cortex and friends) without touching the package DIRECTORIES, which
# are one path segment shorter, nor any source file — no tracked file under
# cmd/*/ begins with "cortex".
agentop
cortex
cortex-envoy
cortex-cpex
authbridge-lite
cortex-praxis
profile-tags
readme-demo
cmd/agentop/agentop
cmd/*/cortex*
scripts/profile-tags/profile-tags
scripts/readme-demo/readme-demo
